cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "lowflow: extreme low-flow (drought) frequency analysis"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
 - family-names: "Niazkar"
    given-names: "Majid"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5022-1026"
    affiliation: "Junior Scientist at Risk Assessment and Adaptation Strategies (RAAS) Department, Euro-Mediterranean Center on Climate Change, Venezia, Italy and Adjunct Professor at Department of Environmental Sciences, Computer Science, and Statistics, Ca’ Foscari University of Venice, Venice, Italy"
repository-code: "https://github.com/majidniazkar/lowflow-frequency-analysis"
license: MIT
version: 1.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-06"
#doi: "<10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX>"
abstract: >-
  Univariate and bivariate frequency analysis of annual and seasonal minimum
  river discharge, in Python and in R. Block-minimum extraction with coverage
  screening, marginal fitting (GEV, Pearson III, Gamma, Weibull) with AIC
  selection and bootstrap goodness-of-fit, low-flow return levels with
  confidence intervals, non-stationary GEV for climate projections, and
  bivariate copulas with AND / OR / Kendall joint return periods.
keywords:
  - hydrology
  - drought
  - low flow
  - extreme value analysis
  - generalised extreme value
  - GEV
  - copula
  - return period
  - 7Q10
